const GUIDES = [
{
  id: "basics",
  icon: "🎲",
  title: {en:"Craps Basics: Dice, Rounds & the Layout", zh:"花旗骰基礎：骰子、回合與賭桌"},
  intro: {en:"Before any strategy, learn how a round actually works and what two dice can really do. Everything in this lab — every edge, every simulation — is built on the 36 combinations below. Get these cold and the rest of the site reads like plain English.",
    zh:"在談任何策略之前，先搞懂一回合怎麼進行、兩顆骰子真正能擲出什麼。本站所有的莊家優勢、所有的模擬，都建立在下面這 36 種組合上。把這些記熟，整站內容就一目了然。"},
  sections: [
    {h:{en:"How a round works", zh:"一回合怎麼進行"},
     body:{en:"<p>Every round starts with a <b>come-out roll</b>. The puck says OFF. On the pass line, 7 or 11 wins (naturals), 2, 3 or 12 loses (craps). Any other number — 4, 5, 6, 8, 9 or 10 — becomes the <b>point</b>, the puck flips to ON, and the game changes.</p><p>Now the shooter rolls until one of two things happens: the point repeats (pass line wins) or a 7 shows (<b>seven-out</b> — pass line loses, dice pass to the next shooter). That loop, come-out → point → decision, is the whole game. Come bets work exactly like pass-line bets, just started after a point is already set.</p><p>On a cruise ship or in Vegas the rhythm is the same — and it's slow. Craps is not a fast game: the dice wait on payouts, center bets, new shooters setting their dice, drink orders and table conversation. A full table typically sees about 40–60 rolls an hour, and a packed, chatty table can be slower still. Only a near-empty table with a fast crew gets anywhere near 100.</p>",
           zh:"<p>每一回合都從<b>開骰首擲</b>開始，點數標記顯示 OFF。過關線注：擲出 7 或 11 直接贏（天胡），2、3 或 12 直接輸（Craps）。其他數字——4、5、6、8、9、10——就成為<b>點數</b>，標記翻到 ON，遊戲進入第二階段。</p><p>接著擲骰者一直擲，直到兩件事之一發生：重複擲出點數（過關線贏），或擲出 7（<b>七點出局</b>——過關線輸，骰子交給下一位）。開骰 → 點數 → 結算，這個循環就是整個遊戲。來注的玩法和過關線完全一樣，只是等點數確立後才下。</p><p>郵輪上或拉斯維加斯節奏都一樣——而且很慢。花旗骰不是快節奏的遊戲：骰子要等賠付、中間注、新擲骰者擺骰、點飲料和桌上聊天。滿桌時一小時通常約 40–60 擲，人多熱鬧時還會更慢。只有近乎空桌、荷官又快，才可能接近 100 擲。</p>"}},
    {h:{en:"The 36 combinations (the only math that matters)", zh:"36 種組合（唯一重要的數學）"},
     body:{en:"<p>Two dice, 36 equally likely combinations — never think of totals as '2 through 12, all equal.' The 7 is the king of the table: 6 ways out of 36 (16.67%). The 6 and 8 have 5 ways each (13.89%); 5 and 9 have 4 (11.11%); 4 and 10 have 3 (8.33%); 3 and 11 have 2 (5.56%); 2 and 12 have 1 each (2.78%).</p><p>Two consequences you'll feel in your wallet: on come-out, naturals (7/11) win 8 times in 36 and craps (2/3/12) lose 4 in 36, with a point set the other 24. And once a point is on, a 4 or 10 only repeats 1 time in 3 tries against the 7 (3 ways vs 6), a 5 or 9 repeats 2 in 5, a 6 or 8 repeats 5 in 11. That asymmetry is what every place-bet payout is priced against.</p><p>Overall, a pass-line bet wins about <b>244 times out of 495 decisions (49.29%)</b> — close to a coin flip, but the missing 0.71% plus the short pays are exactly where the 1.41% edge lives.</p>",
           zh:"<p>兩顆骰子，36 種等機率組合——千萬別把點數總和想成「2 到 12 都一樣」。7 是桌上的王：36 種裡有 6 種（16.67%）。6 和 8 各 5 種（13.89%）；5 和 9 各 4 種（11.11%）；4 和 10 各 3 種（8.33%）；3 和 11 各 2 種（5.56%）；2 和 12 各只有 1 種（2.78%）。</p><p>兩個會直接影響荷包的結論：開骰時，天胡（7/11）36 次贏 8 次，Craps（2/3/12）36 次輸 4 次，另外 24 次確立點數。點數確立後，4 或 10 對上 7 只有 1/3 的重複機率（3 種對 6 種），5 或 9 是 2/5，6 或 8 是 5/11。所有置注的賠付都是針對這種不對稱定價的。</p><p>整體來說，過關線注約 <b>495 次結算贏 244 次（49.29%）</b>——接近丟銅板，但少掉的 0.71% 加上賠付打折，正是 1.41% 莊家優勢的來源。</p>"}},
    {h:{en:"Glossary highlights: the words dealers use", zh:"術語精華：荷官用的詞"},
     body:{en:"<p>Learn these and you'll follow any table conversation: <b>point</b> (the number to repeat), <b>puck ON/OFF</b> (whether we're in come-out), <b>odds</b> (the free extra bet behind your line bet, paid at true odds, 0% edge), <b>place bet</b> (betting a number hits before the 7, paid short of true odds), <b>buy/lay</b> (pay a 5% vig to get true odds on the 4/10 — or bet against a number), <b>hardway</b> (a pair like 4-4; loses to the 7 <i>or</i> the easy way), <b>field</b> (one-roll bet on 2,3,4,9,10,11,12), <b>press/collect</b> (parlay winnings vs pocket them), <b>vig</b> (commission), <b>seven-out</b> (7 with the point on — round over).</p><p>The full 25-term glossary with Traditional Chinese is in the Glossary tab. When a term shows up in a guide, assume the glossary definition.</p>",
           zh:"<p>學會這些，任何桌邊對話都聽得懂：<b>點數</b>（要重複的數字）、<b>點數標記 ON/OFF</b>（是否在開骰階段）、<b>賠率注</b>（線注後面加的免費注，真實賠率，0% 莊家優勢）、<b>置注</b>（賭某數字先於 7 出現，賠付打折）、<b>買注/放注</b>（付 5% 佣金換 4/10 的真實賠率，或反向下注）、<b>硬式注</b>（對子如 4-4；輸給 7 <i>或</i>軟式）、<b>場注</b>（單擲賭 2,3,4,9,10,11,12）、<b>加注/收注</b>（把贏的錢續押 vs 收進口袋）、<b>佣金</b>、<b>七點出局</b>（點數確立後擲出 7——回合結束）。</p><p>完整的 25 個術語中英對照在術語表分頁。指南裡出現的術語，一律以術語表定義為準。</p>"}}
  ],
  mathBox: {en:"<b>The dice table (36 combos):</b><table><tr><th>Total</th><th>Ways</th><th>Probability</th></tr><tr><td>7</td><td>6</td><td>16.67%</td></tr><tr><td>6, 8</td><td>5 each</td><td>13.89%</td></tr><tr><td>5, 9</td><td>4 each</td><td>11.11%</td></tr><tr><td>4, 10</td><td>3 each</td><td>8.33%</td></tr><tr><td>3, 11</td><td>2 each</td><td>5.56%</td></tr><tr><td>2, 12</td><td>1 each</td><td>2.78%</td></tr></table><p>Come-out: 7/11 win 8/36 · 2/3/12 lose 4/36 · point set 24/36.<br>Point repeats vs 7: 4/10 → 1/3 · 5/9 → 2/5 · 6/8 → 5/11.<br>Pass-line win probability: <b>244/495 ≈ 49.29%</b> · edge <b>1.41%</b>.</p>",
    zh:"<b>骰子組合表（36 種）：</b><table><tr><th>總和</th><th>組合數</th><th>機率</th></tr><tr><td>7</td><td>6</td><td>16.67%</td></tr><tr><td>6、8</td><td>各 5</td><td>13.89%</td></tr><tr><td>5、9</td><td>各 4</td><td>11.11%</td></tr><tr><td>4、10</td><td>各 3</td><td>8.33%</td></tr><tr><td>3、11</td><td>各 2</td><td>5.56%</td></tr><tr><td>2、12</td><td>各 1</td><td>2.78%</td></tr></table><p>開骰：7/11 贏 8/36 · 2/3/12 輸 4/36 · 確立點數 24/36。<br>點數對 7 的重複率：4/10 → 1/3 · 5/9 → 2/5 · 6/8 → 5/11。<br>過關線勝率：<b>244/495 ≈ 49.29%</b> · 莊家優勢 <b>1.41%</b>。</p>"},
  verdict: {en:"Learn the dice before the bets. The 7 showing up 1 time in 6 is not a streak, not a mood, not a 'cold table' — it's arithmetic. Every strategy on this site is just a different way of renting exposure to that arithmetic.",
    zh:"先學骰子，再學下注。7 每 6 次出現 1 次不是連莊、不是手氣、不是「冷桌」——是算術。本站所有策略，都只是用不同方式向這套算術租用曝險。"}
},
{
  id: "passcome",
  icon: "🛣️",
  title: {en:"Pass, Come & Odds: The Low-Edge Core", zh:"過關線、來注與賠率：低優勢核心"},
  intro: {en:"If you want action on a craps table with the smallest mathematical cost, this is the whole list: pass line, come bets, and odds behind them. Everything else on the layout charges you more. This tab also covers the Three Point Molly — the textbook way to stack those low-edge bets.",
    zh:"如果想在花旗骰桌上用最小的數學代價玩，全部清單就是：過關線、來注、再加上後面的賠率注。賭桌上其他所有注都收得更貴。本分頁也講 Three Point Molly——把這些低優勢注疊起來的教科書做法。"},
  sections: [
    {h:{en:"Pass line and don't pass", zh:"過關線與不過關"},
     body:{en:"<p><b>Pass line (1.41% edge):</b> bet with the shooter. Come-out: 7/11 wins even money, 2/3/12 loses. Point set: wins if the point repeats before a 7.</p><p><b>Don't pass (1.36% edge):</b> bet against the shooter. Come-out: 2/3 wins, 7/11 loses, <b>12 pushes</b> (that push is the house's cut). Point set: wins if the 7 comes first. Slightly lower edge than pass, but you're rooting for everyone else to lose — know the table vibe before you plant your flag there.</p>",
           zh:"<p><b>過關線（莊家優勢 1.41%）：</b>跟擲骰者同一邊。開骰：7/11 贏等額，2/3/12 輸。確立點數後：點數先重複就贏。</p><p><b>不過關（莊家優勢 1.36%）：</b>跟擲骰者對作。開骰：2/3 贏，7/11 輸，<b>12 和局退注</b>（這個和局就是賭場的抽水）。確立點數後：7 先出現就贏。優勢比過關線略低，但等於盼著全桌輸——下注前先感受一下桌邊氣氛。</p>"}},
    {h:{en:"Come and don't come", zh:"來注與不來注"},
     body:{en:"<p>A <b>come bet</b> is a pass-line bet made after a point is already set: your next roll is its 'come-out' — 7/11 wins, 2/3/12 loses, anything else becomes <i>your</i> point and travels to that number. Same 1.41% edge. <b>Don't come</b> is the mirror (1.36%, 12 pushes on its come-out).</p><p>Why they matter: they let you stack multiple low-edge numbers instead of being stuck with one point per shooter. That's the engine of the Three Point Molly below.</p>",
           zh:"<p><b>來注</b>就是點數確立後才下的過關線注：下一擲是它的「開骰」——7/11 贏，2/3/12 輸，其他數字成為<i>你的</i>點數並移到該號碼上。同樣 1.41% 優勢。<b>不來注</b>是鏡像（1.36%，開骰遇 12 和局）。</p><p>為什麼重要：它讓你可以同時擁有多個低優勢號碼，而不是一位擲骰者只能卡一個點數。這就是下面 Three Point Molly 的引擎。</p>"}},
    {h:{en:"Free odds: the only 0% bet in the casino", zh:"免費賠率注：賭場唯一的 0% 注"},
     body:{en:"<p>Once your pass/come point is set, you may add an <b>odds bet</b> behind it, paid at <b>true odds</b>: 6:5 on 6/8, 3:2 on 5/9, 2:1 on 4/10. Zero house edge — the casino makes nothing on it. It's the best bet in the building and most beginners leave it on the table.</p><p>Two practical rules dealers enforce: odds on 6/8 must be in <b>units of 6</b> (so 6:5 pays cleanly), odds on 5/9 in <b>units of 2</b> (for 3:2); 4/10 takes any unit. And odds are <b>off on the come-out</b> unless you specifically tell the dealer they're working — a free protection most players don't know they have.</p><p>More odds = lower blended edge, because you're diluting the 1.41% flat bet with 0% money. A 3-4-5x table (3x on 4/10, 4x on 5/9, 5x on 6/8) is the common cruise-ship standard.</p>",
           zh:"<p>過關線/來注的點數確立後，可以在後面加<b>賠率注</b>，按<b>真實賠率</b>支付：6/8 賠 6:5，5/9 賠 3:2，4/10 賠 2:1。莊家優勢是零——賭場在這注上一毛不賺。這是整間賭場最好的注，但多數新手根本沒下。</p><p>荷官會執行的兩個實務規則：6/8 的賠率注必須是 <b>6 的倍數</b>（6:5 才付得乾淨），5/9 必須是 <b>2 的倍數</b>（3:2）；4/10 任意單位都行。還有：開骰時賠率注是<b>關閉不生效</b>的，除非你特別交代荷官開著——多數玩家不知道自己有這個免費保護。</p><p>賠率注下得越多，綜合優勢越低，因為你用 0% 的錢稀釋了 1.41% 的本注。3-4-5 倍（4/10 三倍、5/9 四倍、6/8 五倍）是郵輪賭場常見標準。</p>"}},
    {h:{en:"Three Point Molly: the textbook baseline", zh:"Three Point Molly：教科書級基準"},
     body:{en:"<p><b>Mechanics:</b> $10 on the pass line. Once a point is set, $10 come bet. When it travels to a number, a second $10 come bet. <b>Max odds on all three</b> (whatever the house allows). Once three numbers are covered, no new bets until a decision.</p><p><b>Math:</b> each flat bet carries 1.41%; the odds carry 0%. Blended edge: <b>≈0.3–0.5% at 3-4-5x odds, ≈0.18% at 10x, ≈0.02% at 100x</b>. This is the lowest-edge way to have real action spread across the table — the baseline every other strategy on this site gets compared against.</p><p>The trade: odds money is volatile. You'll feel bigger swings than flat-betting, even though the math is kinder. Size your bankroll for the odds you're actually taking, not just the $10 flat bets.</p>",
           zh:"<p><b>玩法：</b>過關線 $10。點數確立後下 $10 來注；移到號碼上後再下第二個 $10 來注。<b>三個號碼都加滿賠率注</b>（賭場允許多少就加多少）。三個號碼都覆蓋後，在結算前不再下新注。</p><p><b>數學：</b>每個本注 1.41%，賠率注 0%。綜合優勢：<b>3-4-5 倍約 0.3–0.5%，10 倍約 0.18%，100 倍約 0.02%</b>。這是全桌鋪開玩法的最低優勢組合——本站其他策略都要跟它比。</p><p>代價：賠率注的錢波動大。雖然數學更友善，體感起伏會比只下本注劇烈。賭本要按你實際下的賠率注來準備，不是只看那 $10 本注。</p>"}}
  ],
  mathBox: {en:"<b>Line + odds math:</b><table><tr><th>Bet</th><th>Pays</th><th>Edge</th></tr><tr><td>Pass line / Come</td><td>1:1</td><td>1.41%</td></tr><tr><td>Don't pass / Don't come</td><td>1:1 (12 pushes)</td><td>1.36%</td></tr><tr><td>Odds (any point)</td><td>true odds</td><td>0%</td></tr><tr><td>Pass + 3-4-5x odds (blended)</td><td>—</td><td>≈0.3–0.5%</td></tr><tr><td>Pass + 10x odds (blended)</td><td>—</td><td>≈0.18%</td></tr><tr><td>Pass + 100x odds (blended)</td><td>—</td><td>≈0.02%</td></tr></table><p>True odds: 6/8 → 6:5 (units of 6) · 5/9 → 3:2 (units of 2) · 4/10 → 2:1.</p>",
    zh:"<b>線注＋賠率注數學：</b><table><tr><th>注種</th><th>賠付</th><th>優勢</th></tr><tr><td>過關線 / 來注</td><td>1:1</td><td>1.41%</td></tr><tr><td>不過關 / 不來注</td><td>1:1（12 和局）</td><td>1.36%</td></tr><tr><td>賠率注（任何點數）</td><td>真實賠率</td><td>0%</td></tr><tr><td>過關線＋3-4-5 倍（綜合）</td><td>—</td><td>≈0.3–0.5%</td></tr><tr><td>過關線＋10 倍（綜合）</td><td>—</td><td>≈0.18%</td></tr><tr><td>過關線＋100 倍（綜合）</td><td>—</td><td>≈0.02%</td></tr></table><p>真實賠率：6/8 → 6:5（6 的倍數）· 5/9 → 3:2（2 的倍數）· 4/10 → 2:1。</p>"},
  verdict: {en:"This is the correct answer to 'how do I play craps cheaply.' Pass or come, max odds, done. It won't beat the house — nothing will — but at 0.3–0.5% blended it's the cheapest entertainment on the felt, and the math says so out loud.",
    zh:"這就是「怎麼玩花旗骰最便宜」的正確答案：過關線或來注，賠率加滿，收工。它打不贏莊家——什麼都打不贏——但綜合 0.3–0.5% 是整張賭桌最便宜的娛樂，數學就擺在那裡。"}
},
{
  id: "placebets",
  icon: "📍",
  title: {en:"Place Bets, Iron Cross & Cover 4", zh:"置注、鐵十字與 Cover 4"},
  intro: {en:"Place bets are the pick-your-number game: choose 4, 5, 6, 8, 9, 10 and get paid when it hits before the 7. They're flexible and fun — and priced worse than line bets. The Iron Cross is the famous 'win on every roll' layout built on top of them. Read the math before the feeling.",
    zh:"置注是自選號碼遊戲：選 4、5、6、8、9、10，數字先於 7 出現就領錢。彈性高、好玩——但定價比線注差。鐵十字（Iron Cross）就是架在置注上的著名「每擲都贏」陣型。先看數學，再談感覺。"},
  sections: [
    {h:{en:"Place bet mechanics and payouts", zh:"置注玩法與賠付"},
     body:{en:"<p>Tell the dealer 'place the 6' and your chips go on the number. It wins if that number rolls before a 7, loses on a 7. Payouts are <b>short of true odds</b> — that's the edge:</p><ul><li><b>6 / 8:</b> pays 7:6 (true odds would be 6:5) — edge <b>1.52%</b>. Must be bet in <b>$6 increments</b> or the 7:6 payoff breaks; a $12 place 6 pays $14.</li><li><b>5 / 9:</b> pays 7:5 — edge <b>4.00%</b>. A $10 place 5 pays $14.</li><li><b>4 / 10:</b> pays 9:5 — edge <b>6.67%</b>. A $10 place 4 pays $18.</li></ul><p>Place bets are <b>off on the come-out</b> by default (not working) unless you ask — same free protection as odds. Say 'my place bets are working' if you want them live during come-out.</p>",
           zh:"<p>跟荷官說「place the 6」，籌碼就放到該號碼上。數字先於 7 出現就贏，7 出現就輸。賠付<b>低於真實賠率</b>——差額就是莊家優勢：</p><ul><li><b>6 / 8：</b>賠 7:6（真實賠率是 6:5）——優勢 <b>1.52%</b>。必須用 <b>$6 為單位</b>下，否則 7:6 付不乾淨；$12 的 6 置注贏 $14。</li><li><b>5 / 9：</b>賠 7:5——優勢 <b>4.00%</b>。$10 的 5 置注贏 $14。</li><li><b>4 / 10：</b>賠 9:5——優勢 <b>6.67%</b>。$10 的 4 置注贏 $18。</li></ul><p>置注在開骰時<b>預設關閉不生效</b>，除非你要求——跟賠率注一樣的免費保護。想在開骰時也生效就說「我的置注要 working」。</p>"}},
    {h:{en:"The Iron Cross: win almost every roll (and pay for it)", zh:"鐵十字：幾乎每擲都贏（然後付出代價）"},
     body:{en:"<p><b>Mechanics:</b> after come-out, place the 5, 6 and 8 (e.g. $5/$6/$6) and add a $5 field bet. The field covers 2, 3, 4, 9, 10, 11, 12; the places cover 5, 6, 8. Every number except 7 pays something — the 'win almost every roll' feeling is real.</p><p><b>Math:</b> blended edge ≈ <b>3–4%</b> (field at 5.56% on 2x/2x tables or 2.78% where 12 pays triple; place 5 at 4%; 6/8 at 1.52%). And the 7 — 6 ways in 36, <b>16.67% of rolls</b> — wipes the entire layout at once. Small wins drip in; the 7 takes them back in one roll. Run it in the Batch Lab and watch the equity curve: a slow bleed with cliffs.</p><p>It's genuinely fun, especially on a lively cruise table. Just know the price: roughly 3–4% per dollar of action, versus 0.3–0.5% for a 3-Point Molly.</p>",
           zh:"<p><b>玩法：</b>開骰後置注 5、6、8（例如 $5/$6/$6），再加 $5 場注。場注覆蓋 2、3、4、9、10、11、12；置注覆蓋 5、6、8。除了 7 之外每個數字都付錢——「幾乎每擲都贏」的感覺是真的。</p><p><b>數學：</b>綜合優勢約 <b>3–4%</b>（場注在 2 倍賠付桌是 5.56%，12 賠三倍的桌是 2.78%；5 置注 4%；6/8 置注 1.52%）。而 7——36 種裡 6 種，<b>佔每次擲骰 16.67%</b>——一次清掉整張版面。小贏慢慢滴進來，7 一次全部拿回去。去批量實驗室跑跑看權益曲線：緩慢失血，間或斷崖。</p><p>它真的好玩，尤其在熱鬧的郵輪賭桌上。只要知道價格：每單位投注約 3–4%，對比 Three Point Molly 的 0.3–0.5%。</p>"}},
    {h:{en:"Cover 4: press, collect, or flat?", zh:"Cover 4：加注、收注，還是不動？"},
     body:{en:"<p>Cover-4 style systems place four numbers with a rule for what happens after a hit: <b>press</b> (parlay the winnings into a bigger bet), <b>collect</b> (pocket the winnings), or <b>flat</b> (leave the bet alone). Table language: after a hit, say <b>'same bet'</b> to keep it, <b>'press it up one unit'</b> to add a unit, <b>'press it up all the way'</b> to double it, or <b>'regress'</b> to drop the bet down and pocket the difference.</p><p><b>Math:</b> pressing changes variance, not expectation. Every pressed dollar still faces the same place-bet edge (1.52–6.67%). Pressing feels like 'playing with house money' — the house money is still yours, and it's still taxed at the place-bet rate. The Batch Lab's killer view: same layout, three money modes, overlaid equity curves.</p><p>Player archetypes dealers joke about: <b>Bulls</b> press immediately, <b>Bears</b> regress after a hit or two and press only when hot, <b>Pigs</b> never take profits — 'pigs get slaughtered.'</p>",
           zh:"<p>Cover 4 這類系統在四個號碼下置注，並規定中獎後怎麼做：<b>加注</b>（把贏的錢續押放大注碼）、<b>收注</b>（把贏的錢收進口袋）、或<b>不動</b>（注碼維持原樣）。桌邊術語：中獎後說 <b>「same bet」</b>維持原注，<b>「press it up one unit」</b>加一個單位，<b>「press it up all the way」</b>直接翻倍，<b>「regress」</b>降注並把差額收走。</p><p><b>數學：</b>加注改變的是波動，不是期望值。加注的每一塊錢面對的還是同樣的置注優勢（1.52–6.67%）。加注感覺像「用莊家的錢玩」——那錢還是你的，而且照樣被置注稅率抽。批量實驗室最強的視角：同一陣型，三種資金模式，權益曲線疊在一起看。</p><p>荷官私下笑稱的玩家類型：<b>公牛</b>立刻加注，<b>熊</b>中一兩次後降注、只在熱的時候加，<b>豬</b>從不收錢——「豬註定被宰」。</p>"}}
  ],
  mathBox: {en:"<b>Place-bet edges:</b><table><tr><th>Bet</th><th>Pays</th><th>Edge</th></tr><tr><td>Place 6 / 8</td><td>7:6</td><td>1.52%</td></tr><tr><td>Place 5 / 9</td><td>7:5</td><td>4.00%</td></tr><tr><td>Place 4 / 10</td><td>9:5</td><td>6.67%</td></tr><tr><td>Iron Cross (blended)</td><td>—</td><td>≈3–4%</td></tr></table><p>The 7 wipes an Iron Cross/Cover layout <b>16.67%</b> of rolls (6/36). Pressing never changes these numbers — it only changes the shape of the ride.</p>",
    zh:"<b>置注優勢表：</b><table><tr><th>注種</th><th>賠付</th><th>優勢</th></tr><tr><td>置注 6 / 8</td><td>7:6</td><td>1.52%</td></tr><tr><td>置注 5 / 9</td><td>7:5</td><td>4.00%</td></tr><tr><td>置注 4 / 10</td><td>9:5</td><td>6.67%</td></tr><tr><td>鐵十字（綜合）</td><td>—</td><td>≈3–4%</td></tr></table><p>7 每擲有 <b>16.67%</b> 機率（6/36）一次清掉鐵十字/Cover 版面。加注永遠改變不了這些數字——只改變過程的形狀。</p>"},
  verdict: {en:"Place bets are how you buy fun at a fair-ish price — the 6/8 at 1.52% is honest entertainment. The Iron Cross is the same fun with a 3–4% cover charge and a 16.67%-per-roll guillotine. Enjoy it with eyes open, collect sometimes, and never mistake 'wins most rolls' for 'wins money.'",
    zh:"置注是用還算公道的價格買樂趣——6/8 的 1.52% 是誠實的娛樂。鐵十字是同樣的樂趣，但收 3–4% 的入場費，外加每擲 16.67% 的斷頭台。睜著眼睛享受，記得收錢，永遠別把「多數擲骰都贏」誤會成「贏錢」。"}
},
{
  id: "progressions",
  icon: "📈",
  title: {en:"Progressions: Martingale & 1-3-2-5", zh:"倍注法：馬丁格爾與 1-3-2-5"},
  intro: {en:"Progressions don't change the edge — they rearrange it. Many small wins with a rare disaster, or small losses chasing a rare celebration. Understand the shape before you ride it, because the disaster is priced into the math whether you feel it or not.",
    zh:"倍注法改變不了莊家優勢——只能重新排列它。多數小贏配一次罕見災難，或小輸追一次罕見慶祝。上車前先看懂這個形狀，因為災難已經定價在數學裡，不管你有沒有感覺。"},
  sections: [
    {h:{en:"Martingale: double after every loss", zh:"馬丁格爾：輸了就加倍"},
     body:{en:"<p><b>Mechanics:</b> bet 1 unit on an ~even-money wager (pass line). Lose → double. Lose again → double again. Win → back to 1 unit. One win recovers all previous losses plus 1 unit of profit. Feels like free money — until it isn't.</p><p><b>Math:</b> the edge stays <b>1.41%</b> on every dollar. What changes is the distribution: most sessions end a few units up, a few end in ruin. A 7-loss streak on the pass line happens about <b>0.83% of the time</b> per 7-decision sequence — rare per sequence, near-certain over a long trip. And the table maximum is the real killer: after 6–7 doublings you can't double again, which is exactly when you need to.</p><p>Run 100,000 Martingale bots in the Batch Lab and look at the <i>worst</i> cases, not the average. The signature shape: a cliff. Most bots profit; a few are destroyed. That tail is the price of all those small wins.</p>",
           zh:"<p><b>玩法：</b>在約等額注（過關線）下 1 單位。輸 → 加倍。再輸 → 再加倍。贏 → 回到 1 單位。一次贏就收回前面所有虧損外加 1 單位利潤。感覺像免費的錢——直到不是為止。</p><p><b>數學：</b>每一塊錢的優勢還是 <b>1.41%</b>。改變的是分佈：多數 session 小贏幾個單位，少數直接破產。過關線連輸 7 次，每 7 次結算約發生 <b>0.83%</b>——單看很罕見，長期玩下來幾乎必然遇到。真正的殺手是桌檯上限：加倍 6–7 次後就加不動了，而那正是最需要加倍的時候。</p><p>去批量實驗室跑 100,000 個馬丁格爾機器人，看<i>最慘</i>的案例，不要只看平均。標誌性形狀：一座斷崖。多數機器人賺錢，少數被摧毀。那條尾巴就是所有小贏的代價。</p>"}},
    {h:{en:"1-3-2-5: the positive progression", zh:"1-3-2-5：正向倍注法"},
     body:{en:"<p><b>Mechanics:</b> on an even-money bet, wager <b>1 unit, then 3, then 2, then 5</b>. Win all four in a row and you've turned 1 unit of risk into +11 units of profit (a variant of the classic 1-3-2-6). <b>Reset to 1 unit after any loss — or after completing the sequence.</b> Lose at the '3' step and you're only down 2 units net (won 1, lost 3); lose at '2' and you're still up 2 net. The design goal: survive the early steps, get paid on the late ones.</p><p><b>Math:</b> still 1.41% per dollar — a positive progression just concentrates your big bets into the moments after wins. It needs win streaks to pay, and streaks are exactly what the dice don't owe you. Honest framing: it's a fun way to structure a session, not a way to manufacture profit.</p><p>Compare it against flat betting the same base unit in the Batch Lab. Same edge, spikier ride.</p>",
           zh:"<p><b>玩法：</b>在等額注上依序下 <b>1 單位、3 單位、2 單位、5 單位</b>。連贏四把，1 單位的風險變成 +11 單位利潤（經典 1-3-2-6 的變體）。<b>任何一次輸、或走完序列，都重回 1 單位。</b>在「3」那步輸，淨虧 2 單位（贏 1 輸 3）；在「2」那步輸，淨賺還是 +2。設計目標：前面幾步活下來，後面幾步領錢。</p><p><b>數學：</b>每塊錢還是 1.41%——正向倍注只是把大注集中在連贏之後。要賺錢需要連贏，而骰子從不欠你連贏。誠實的說法：這是讓 session 好玩的結構，不是製造利潤的方法。</p><p>去批量實驗室把它和同單位的平注對比：同樣的優勢，更刺激的雲霄飛車。</p>"}},
    {h:{en:"The language: press, collect, regress", zh:"術語：加注、收注、降注"},
     body:{en:"<p>After any place bet hits, the dealer waits for your call. <b>'Same bet'</b> — leave it. <b>'Press it up one unit'</b> — add one unit from the winnings. <b>'Press it up all the way'</b> — double the bet (the classic squeeze move on a busy table). <b>'Regress'</b> — drop to a smaller bet and pocket the difference. No call usually means same bet, but on a loud table, say it clearly.</p><p>Remember the archetypes: <b>Bulls</b> press immediately, <b>Bears</b> regress after a hit or two, <b>Pigs</b> never collect — and pigs get slaughtered. Decide <i>before</i> the roll which one you are tonight, because the table will decide for you otherwise.</p>",
           zh:"<p>任何置注中獎後，荷官會等你指令。<b>「Same bet」</b>——維持原注。<b>「Press it up one unit」</b>——從贏的錢加一個單位。<b>「Press it up all the way」</b>——直接翻倍（忙碌賭桌上的經典快手）。<b>「Regress」</b>——降到小注，把差額收走。桌上太吵時，沒指令通常視為維持原注，所以要講清楚。</p><p>記住三種動物：<b>公牛</b>立刻加注，<b>熊</b>中一兩次後降注，<b>豬</b>從不收錢——豬註定被宰。今晚開骰前先決定自己是哪一種，不然賭桌會幫你決定。</p>"}}
  ],
  mathBox: {en:"<b>Progression math:</b><table><tr><th>System</th><th>Edge per $</th><th>Key number</th></tr><tr><td>Martingale (pass line)</td><td>1.41% (unchanged)</td><td>7-loss streak ≈ 0.83% per 7 decisions</td></tr><tr><td>1-3-2-5 (even money)</td><td>1.41% (unchanged)</td><td>Full sequence: +11 units on 1 unit risk</td></tr></table><p>A '97% win rate' system can still have negative expectation — small frequent wins vs rare disasters. Always ask for the expected value next to the win rate.</p>",
    zh:"<b>倍注法數學：</b><table><tr><th>系統</th><th>每元優勢</th><th>關鍵數字</th></tr><tr><td>馬丁格爾（過關線）</td><td>1.41%（不變）</td><td>連輸 7 次每 7 結算約 0.83%</td></tr><tr><td>1-3-2-5（等額注）</td><td>1.41%（不變）</td><td>走完序列：1 單位風險換 +11 單位</td></tr></table><p>「97% 勝率」的系統期望值照樣可以是負的——高頻小贏 vs 罕見災難。看到勝率，一定要同時問期望值。</p>"},
  verdict: {en:"Progressions are money management, not edge management. They decide <i>when</i> you lose, not <i>whether</i>. If the shape of the ride is worth the price to you — small steady wins with a known cliff — play it knowingly. Never play one believing the doubling 'covers' the edge. The Batch Lab's worst-case view exists precisely for this tab.",
    zh:"倍注法是資金管理，不是優勢管理。它決定你<i>何時</i>輸，不決定你<i>輸不輸</i>。如果你覺得這個形狀值這個價——穩定小贏配一座已知的斷崖——那就清醒地玩。永遠別相信加倍能「覆蓋」莊家優勢。批量實驗室的最慘案例視角，正是為這個分頁而生的。"}
}
];

GUIDES.push(
{
  id: "hedge",
  icon: "🛡️",
  title: {en:"The Arnold & Hedge Systems", zh:"The Arnold 與對沖系統"},
  intro: {en:"Betting both sides of the same coin feels clever — 'I win either way!' You don't. Hedging in craps doesn't cancel the edge; it stacks two edges and pays the house twice. The Arnold is the cleanest example of why.",
    zh:"同時下同一枚硬幣的兩面感覺很聰明——「兩邊都贏！」並沒有。在花旗骰對沖不會抵銷莊家優勢；它是疊了兩個優勢，讓賭場收兩次錢。The Arnold 是最好的示範。"},
  sections: [
    {h:{en:"The Arnold: mechanics", zh:"The Arnold：玩法"},
     body:{en:"<p><b>Mechanics:</b> 1 unit on the pass line. Once the point is established, put <b>4 units on don't come</b>. Then place 1-unit come bets every roll until seven-out or the don't-come bet comes down; if the don't come falls, replace it and repeat.</p><p>So you're rooting <i>for</i> the shooter with 1 unit and <i>against</i> the shooter with 4 units, plus a stream of small come bets. It looks like a hedged, 'balanced' position. Watch what the math does to that balance.</p>",
           zh:"<p><b>玩法：</b>過關線下 1 單位。點數確立後，在不來注下 <b>4 單位</b>。之後每擲都下 1 單位來注，直到七點出局或不來注結算；不來注掉了就補上重來。</p><p>等於用 1 單位挺擲骰者、用 4 單位反擲骰者，再加一串小來注。看起來是對沖好的「平衡」部位。來看看數學怎麼拆這個平衡。</p>"}},
    {h:{en:"Why hedging multiplies your costs", zh:"為什麼對沖是成本加倍"},
     body:{en:"<p>Pass (1.41%) and don't come (1.36%) are opposite sides of the same coin. When both are live, on most rolls one wins and the other loses — you churn dollars through <i>two</i> house edges instead of one. The 4-unit don't come dominates the position, so The Arnold behaves like a don't-side grind with extra variance from the come bets layered on top.</p><p>The general rule: <b>every hedge is two bets, and the house collects on both.</b> The pass/don't-pass pair, the 'bet the 6 and lay the 6' pair, the field-plus-place overlaps in the Iron Cross — none of them reduce the edge. They just make the losses quieter and the wins smaller, which is exactly why they feel safe.</p><p>If you want the don't side, just play the don't side (don't pass + don't come + lay the odds — odds on don't are also 0%). Don't pay for both sides of the coin.</p>",
           zh:"<p>過關線（1.41%）和不來注（1.36%）是同一枚硬幣的兩面。兩邊同時生效時，多數擲骰一邊贏一邊輸——你的錢在<i>兩個</i>莊家優勢裡空轉，而不是一個。4 單位的不來注主導整個部位，所以 The Arnold 本質上是反向磨局，只是上面疊了來注多一點波動。</p><p>通用法則：<b>每個對沖都是兩筆注，賭場兩筆都收錢。</b>過關/不過關配對、「6 置注加放注 6」、鐵十字裡場注和置注的重疊——沒有一個能降低優勢。它們只是讓虧損更安靜、讓獲利更小，這正是感覺安全的原因。</p><p>想玩反向就直接玩反向（不過關＋不來注＋放賠率注——反向的賠率注一樣是 0%）。別為一枚硬幣的兩面都付錢。</p>"}}
  ],
  mathBox: {en:"<b>Hedge math:</b><table><tr><th>Side</th><th>Edge</th></tr><tr><td>Pass / Come</td><td>1.41%</td></tr><tr><td>Don't pass / Don't come</td><td>1.36%</td></tr></table><p>The Arnold ≈ a 4-unit don't-side grind + 1-unit pass + come-bet noise. Two live opposite bets = two edges collected. No combination of hedges reduces total edge exposure — it increases it.</p>",
    zh:"<b>對沖數學：</b><table><tr><th>方向</th><th>優勢</th></tr><tr><td>過關線 / 來注</td><td>1.41%</td></tr><tr><td>不過關 / 不來注</td><td>1.36%</td></tr></table><p>The Arnold ≈ 4 單位反向磨局 ＋ 1 單位過關線 ＋ 來注雜訊。兩筆對作的注同時生效＝賭場收兩次優勢。任何對沖組合都不會降低總優勢曝險——只會增加。</p>"},
  verdict: {en:"The Arnold looks like engineering and acts like a donation with extra steps. If the idea of 'never losing big' appeals to you, the honest version is smaller bets on one side — not bigger bets on both.",
    zh:"The Arnold 看起來像工程，實際是多幾道手續的捐款。如果「不要大輸」吸引你，誠實的版本是單邊下小注——不是兩邊都下大注。"}
},
{
  id: "bonusbets",
  icon: "🎰",
  title: {en:"Bonus & Prop Bets: Lottery Tickets on the Felt", zh:"紅利注與單擲注：賭桌上的樂透"},
  intro: {en:"ATS, Fire, hardways, horn, hop — the bets with the big glowing payouts and the quiet big edges. They're fun the way lottery tickets are fun. This tab prices every one of them honestly, so if you play them, you know exactly what the ticket costs.",
    zh:"ATS、Fire、硬式注、號角、跳注——賠付閃閃發光、莊家優勢安靜地高的注。好玩的程度跟樂透一樣。本分頁把每一種都誠實定價，讓你下注時清楚知道這張票多少錢。"},
  sections: [
    {h:{en:"ATS: All / Tall / Small", zh:"ATS：全數 / 高數 / 低數"},
     body:{en:"<p><b>Mechanics:</b> usually $1 on each of three circles. <b>Small</b> wins if the shooter rolls 2, 3, 4, 5 and 6 before sevening out; <b>Tall</b> needs 8, 9, 10, 11, 12; <b>All</b> needs every number except 7. Most casinos require a pass-line bet on come-out to play it (you can usually pull the line bet down after).</p><p><b>Math (verified):</b> P(Small or Tall) ≈ <b>2.635%</b> — about 1 in 38 shooters. P(All) ≈ <b>0.5258%</b> — about 1 in 190 shooters. Typical pays of 34:1 / 174:1 work out to a house edge of ≈<b>7.76%</b>. A $1 'all' that hits returns $175 total ($174 profit + your $1 back). Fun? Absolutely. An investment? It's a lottery ticket with a 7.76% service charge.</p><p>The simulator can answer the real question: 'how many shooters until it hits?' — usually far more than your session has.</p>",
           zh:"<p><b>玩法：</b>通常三個圈各 $1。<b>低數</b>（Small）要擲骰者在七點出局前擲出 2、3、4、5、6；<b>高數</b>（Tall）要 8、9、10、11、12；<b>全數</b>（All）要除了 7 之外的每個數字。多數賭場要求開骰時有過關線注才能玩（之後通常可以把線注收回）。</p><p><b>數學（已驗證）：</b>中小/高數機率約 <b>2.635%</b>——約 38 位擲骰者中 1 位。全數約 <b>0.5258%</b>——約 190 位中 1 位。常見賠付 34:1 / 174:1，莊家優勢約 <b>7.76%</b>。$1 全數中了總共拿回 $175（$174 利潤＋$1 本金）。好玩嗎？超好玩。是投資嗎？是收 7.76% 手續費的樂透。</p><p>模擬器能回答真正的問題：「要幾位擲骰者才會中一次？」——通常比你的 session 撐得久得多。</p>"}},
    {h:{en:"Fire bet and Repeater", zh:"Fire 注與 Repeater"},
     body:{en:"<p><b>Fire bet:</b> pays when the shooter makes multiple <i>different</i> points before sevening out (typical paytable 24 / 249 / 999 for 4, 5, 6 points). Edge ≈ <b>20%+</b> — one of the worst bets on the layout, priced like a carnival game.</p><p><b>Repeater:</b> pays when the shooter repeats specific numbers before seven-out. Paytables vary table to table — and that variance is the warning: always read the paytable before touching it. Edges run high, in the same lottery-ticket family as ATS and Fire. If you can't find the paytable printed on the felt, treat that as your answer.</p>",
           zh:"<p><b>Fire 注：</b>擲骰者在七點出局前做出多個<i>不同</i>點數就賠付（常見賠付表 4、5、6 個點數賠 24 / 249 / 999）。優勢約 <b>20%+</b>——整張賭桌最差的注之一，定價跟嘉年華遊戲一樣。</p><p><b>Repeater：</b>擲骰者在七點出局前重複擲出特定數字就賠付。賠付表每桌不同——這本身就是警告：下注前一定先看賠付表。優勢很高，跟 ATS、Fire 同屬樂透家族。如果賠付表沒印在賭桌上，那就把這件事當作答案。</p>"}},
    {h:{en:"Hardways: the pair bets", zh:"硬式注：對子注"},
     body:{en:"<p><b>Mechanics:</b> bet that 4, 6, 8 or 10 rolls as a <b>pair</b> (2-2, 3-3, 4-4, 5-5) before the 7 <i>or</i> the easy way (e.g. hard 8 loses to 7 <i>and</i> to 6-2 or 5-3). It's a standing bet — stays up until it wins or loses, through come-outs.</p><p><b>Math:</b> hard 4 / hard 10 pay <b>7:1</b> at <b>11.11%</b> edge; hard 6 / hard 8 pay <b>9:1</b> at <b>9.09%</b> edge. A $5 hard 8 pays $45. Dealers love tipping action on hardways ('$1 hard 8 for the boys') because the math loves it too — for the house.</p>",
           zh:"<p><b>玩法：</b>賭 4、6、8、10 以<b>對子</b>出現（2-2、3-3、4-4、5-5），先於 7 <i>或</i>軟式（例如硬 8 輸給 7，<i>也</i>輸給 6-2、5-3）。是常駐注——中獎或輸掉之前一直留著，跨開骰。</p><p><b>數學：</b>硬 4 / 硬 10 賠 <b>7:1</b>，優勢 <b>11.11%</b>；硬 6 / 硬 8 賠 <b>9:1</b>，優勢 <b>9.09%</b>。$5 硬 8 贏 $45。荷官喜歡客人用硬式注打賞（「$1 硬 8 給你們」），因為數學也喜歡——喜歡的是莊家那邊。</p>"}},
    {h:{en:"One-roll props: seven, craps, horn, hop, C&E", zh:"單擲注：七點、Craps、號角、跳注、C&E"},
     body:{en:"<p>The center of the table is the expensive neighborhood. One roll, win or lose:</p><ul><li><b>Any seven:</b> pays 4:1, edge <b>16.67%</b> — the worst commonly-offered bet in the casino. A $5 any-seven pays $20.</li><li><b>Any craps (2/3/12):</b> pays 7:1, edge <b>11.11%</b>. A $3 any-craps on the 12 pays $21 profit.</li><li><b>Horn (2,3,11,12):</b> $1 on each; 2/12 pay 30:1, 3/11 pay 15:1; edge <b>12.5%</b>. A $4 horn with the 2 hitting nets $27 ($30 minus the $3 in losers).</li><li><b>Hop:</b> call the exact dice (e.g. '5-5'). Hard (1-way) pays 30:1 at <b>13.89%</b>; easy (2-way) pays 15:1 at <b>11.11%</b>. A $2 hard hop on 5-5 pays $60.</li><li><b>C&E (craps + eleven):</b> split bet, half on any craps (7:1), half on 11 (15:1); edge 11.11%. A $4 C&E with 11 hitting nets $28 ($30 minus the $2 craps half).</li><li><b>Big 6 / Big 8:</b> even money that 6 or 8 rolls before 7 — edge <b>9.09%</b>. Never take it; place the 6/8 instead (1.52%).</li></ul>",
           zh:"<p>賭桌中央是貴价地段。單擲定輸贏：</p><ul><li><b>任意七點：</b>賠 4:1，優勢 <b>16.67%</b>——賭場常見注裡最差的。$5 任意七點贏 $20。</li><li><b>任意 Craps（2/3/12）：</b>賠 7:1，優勢 <b>11.11%</b>。$3 任意 Craps 中 12 贏 $21 利潤。</li><li><b>號角注（2、3、11、12）：</b>各 $1；2/12 賠 30:1，3/11 賠 15:1；優勢 <b>12.5%</b>。$4 號角注中 2 淨賺 $27（$30 減掉 $3 輸掉的）。</li><li><b>跳注：</b>指定骰面（例如「5-5」）。硬跳（1 種組合）賠 30:1，優勢 <b>13.89%</b>；軟跳（2 種組合）賠 15:1，優勢 <b>11.11%</b>。$2 硬跳 5-5 贏 $60。</li><li><b>C&E（Craps 加 11）：</b>對半分注，一半任意 Craps（7:1）、一半 11（15:1）；優勢 11.11%。$4 C&E 中 11 淨賺 $28（$30 減掉輸掉的 $2 Craps 那半）。</li><li><b>大 6 / 大 8：</b>賭 6 或 8 先於 7 出現，賠等額——優勢 <b>9.09%</b>。永遠別下；改置注 6/8（1.52%）。</li></ul>"}}
  ],
  mathBox: {en:"<b>Bonus & prop edges (honest prices):</b><table><tr><th>Bet</th><th>Pays</th><th>Edge</th></tr><tr><td>ATS Small / Tall</td><td>34:1</td><td>≈7.76%</td></tr><tr><td>ATS All</td><td>174:1</td><td>≈7.76%</td></tr><tr><td>Fire bet</td><td>24/249/999</td><td>≈20%+</td></tr><tr><td>Hard 4 / 10</td><td>7:1</td><td>11.11%</td></tr><tr><td>Hard 6 / 8</td><td>9:1</td><td>9.09%</td></tr><tr><td>Any seven</td><td>4:1</td><td>16.67%</td></tr><tr><td>Any craps</td><td>7:1</td><td>11.11%</td></tr><tr><td>Horn</td><td>30:1 / 15:1</td><td>12.50%</td></tr><tr><td>Hop hard / easy</td><td>30:1 / 15:1</td><td>13.89% / 11.11%</td></tr><tr><td>Big 6 / 8</td><td>1:1</td><td>9.09%</td></tr></table>",
    zh:"<b>紅利注與單擲注優勢（誠實定價）：</b><table><tr><th>注種</th><th>賠付</th><th>優勢</th></tr><tr><td>ATS 低數 / 高數</td><td>34:1</td><td>≈7.76%</td></tr><tr><td>ATS 全數</td><td>174:1</td><td>≈7.76%</td></tr><tr><td>Fire 注</td><td>24/249/999</td><td>≈20%+</td></tr><tr><td>硬 4 / 10</td><td>7:1</td><td>11.11%</td></tr><tr><td>硬 6 / 8</td><td>9:1</td><td>9.09%</td></tr><tr><td>任意七點</td><td>4:1</td><td>16.67%</td></tr><tr><td>任意 Craps</td><td>7:1</td><td>11.11%</td></tr><tr><td>號角注</td><td>30:1 / 15:1</td><td>12.50%</td></tr><tr><td>跳注 硬/軟</td><td>30:1 / 15:1</td><td>13.89% / 11.11%</td></tr><tr><td>大 6 / 8</td><td>1:1</td><td>9.09%</td></tr></table>"},
  verdict: {en:"Play these like lottery tickets: tiny, for fun, with zero expectation. A $1 ATS is a fine story for a dollar. A $25 hardway habit is a second rent payment to the casino. The glowing payout is the marketing; the edge column above is the product.",
    zh:"把這些當樂透玩：小注、好玩、零期待。$1 的 ATS 是花一塊錢買個故事。$25 的硬式注習慣是每個月多繳一次房租給賭場。閃閃發光的賠付是廣告；上面的優勢欄才是產品。"}
},
{
  id: "variants",
  icon: "🔀",
  title: {en:"Crapless Craps: The Full Deep-Dive", zh:"無敗骰：完整深潛"},
  intro: {en:"'You can't lose on the come-out!' — true, and it's the most expensive sentence on the felt. Crapless craps turns 2, 3, 4, 10, 11 and 12 into points. Only the 7 wins on come-out; the 11 no longer wins. Here's what that really costs, and the one genuinely good bet hiding in the variant.",
    zh:"「開骰不會輸！」——真的，也是賭桌上最貴的一句話。無敗骰把 2、3、4、10、11、12 都變成點數。開骰只有 7 會贏，11 不再贏。下面是真正的代價，以及藏在這個變體裡唯一真正好的注。"},
  sections: [
    {h:{en:"What changes on a crapless layout", zh:"無敗骰桌改變了什麼"},
     body:{en:"<p>On come-out, <b>only the 7 wins</b> on pass (6/36). The 2, 3, 4, 10, 11 and 12 all become <b>points</b> — including the extremes, 2 and 12, which each have exactly 1 way in 36. The 11, which used to be an instant winner, is now just another point to grind.</p><p>The pitch is 'turn the dice in your favor.' The data says the opposite: pass-line edge jumps from 1.41% to <b>5.38%</b>, and don't pass goes from 1.36% to ≈<b>2.3%</b>. You traded come-out losses for a table full of terrible points.</p>",
           zh:"<p>開骰時，過關線<b>只有 7 會贏</b>（36 種裡 6 種）。2、3、4、10、11、12 全部變成<b>點數</b>——包括 2 和 12 這兩個極端，各只有 36 分之 1 的組合。11 本來是直接贏，現在只是另一個要磨的點數。</p><p>宣傳詞是「讓骰子站在你這邊」。數據說相反：過關線優勢從 1.41% 跳到 <b>5.38%</b>，不過關從 1.36% 變成約 <b>2.3%</b>。你用開骰的虧損，換來整桌難纏的點數。</p>"}},
    {h:{en:"The extreme points: place and buy math", zh:"極端點數：置注與買注數學"},
     body:{en:"<p>The 2/12 and 3/11 can be <b>placed</b>: place 2/12 pays <b>11:2</b> at <b>7.14%</b> edge; place 3/11 pays <b>11:4</b> at <b>6.25%</b> edge. Worse than regular place bets — skip.</p><p>But they can also be <b>bought</b>, and this is where crapless hides its secret. With <b>commission charged only on wins</b>: buy 2/12 pays <b>119:20</b> (≈5.95:1, true odds would be 6:1) at ≈<b>0.71%</b> edge; buy 3/11 pays <b>59:20</b> at ≈<b>1.25%</b> edge. Those are genuinely good bets — better than a regular place 6/8. With commission charged <b>always</b> (upfront), both jump to ≈<b>4.76%</b> — so the exact vig rule is everything. Ask the dealer: 'is the commission only on wins?' before you touch these.</p>",
           zh:"<p>2/12 和 3/11 可以<b>置注</b>：置注 2/12 賠 <b>11:2</b>，優勢 <b>7.14%</b>；置注 3/11 賠 <b>11:4</b>，優勢 <b>6.25%</b>。比一般置注還差——跳過。</p><p>但它們也可以<b>買注</b>，這就是無敗骰藏的秘密。<b>只在贏時收佣金</b>的情況下：買 2/12 賠 <b>119:20</b>（約 5.95:1，真實賠率是 6:1），優勢約 <b>0.71%</b>；買 3/11 賠 <b>59:20</b>，優勢約 <b>1.25%</b>。這是真正好的注——比一般置注 6/8 還好。如果佣金<b>每次都收</b>（預付），兩者都跳到約 <b>4.76%</b>——所以佣金規則就是一切。下注前先問荷官：「佣金是只在贏的時候收嗎？」</p>"}},
    {h:{en:"The 'anything but 7' flaw", zh:"「除了 7 全下」的結構缺陷"},
     body:{en:"<p>The tempting crapless system: bet across <b>every number</b> so only the 7 loses — 'anything but 7!' It has the exact structural flaw of the Iron Cross, with worse per-bet edges: the 7 appears <b>16.67%</b> of rolls (6/36) and wipes the entire layout in one roll. Every other roll pays small; the 7 collects.</p><p>Compare honestly: Iron Cross blends ≈3–4% with the same 16.67% guillotine. The crapless version blends worse because the extreme points carry 6–7% place edges (or 0.71–1.25% if you buy them right — but almost nobody does). 'Can't lose on come-out' cost you the whole game.</p>",
           zh:"<p>無敗骰最誘人的系統：<b>每個數字都下</b>，只有 7 會輸——「除了 7 什麼都行！」它有跟鐵十字完全相同的結構缺陷，只是每個注的優勢更差：7 每擲出現率 <b>16.67%</b>（6/36），一次清掉整張版面。其他每次都小贏，7 來了全部收走。</p><p>誠實對比：鐵十字綜合約 3–4%，斷頭台同樣是 16.67%。無敗骰版本綜合更差，因為極端點數的置注優勢是 6–7%（買對的話是 0.71–1.25%，但幾乎沒人這樣買）。「開骰不會輸」這句話，代價是整場遊戲。</p>"}}
  ],
  mathBox: {en:"<b>Crapless edges:</b><table><tr><th>Bet</th><th>Pays</th><th>Edge</th></tr><tr><td>Pass line</td><td>1:1</td><td>5.38%</td></tr><tr><td>Don't pass</td><td>1:1</td><td>≈2.3%</td></tr><tr><td>Place 2 / 12</td><td>11:2</td><td>7.14%</td></tr><tr><td>Place 3 / 11</td><td>11:4</td><td>6.25%</td></tr><tr><td>Buy 2/12, vig only on wins</td><td>119:20</td><td>≈0.71%</td></tr><tr><td>Buy 3/11, vig only on wins</td><td>59:20</td><td>≈1.25%</td></tr><tr><td>Buy 2/12 or 3/11, vig always</td><td>119:21 / 59:21</td><td>≈4.76%</td></tr></table><p>'Anything but 7' layouts get wiped by the 7 at <b>16.67%</b> per roll — same guillotine as the Iron Cross, worse edges underneath.</p>",
    zh:"<b>無敗骰優勢表：</b><table><tr><th>注種</th><th>賠付</th><th>優勢</th></tr><tr><td>過關線</td><td>1:1</td><td>5.38%</td></tr><tr><td>不過關</td><td>1:1</td><td>≈2.3%</td></tr><tr><td>置注 2 / 12</td><td>11:2</td><td>7.14%</td></tr><tr><td>置注 3 / 11</td><td>11:4</td><td>6.25%</td></tr><tr><td>買 2/12，只贏收佣</td><td>119:20</td><td>≈0.71%</td></tr><tr><td>買 3/11，只贏收佣</td><td>59:20</td><td>≈1.25%</td></tr><tr><td>買 2/12 或 3/11，每次收佣</td><td>119:21 / 59:21</td><td>≈4.76%</td></tr></table><p>「除了 7 全下」的版面每擲有 <b>16.67%</b> 被 7 清掉——跟鐵十字同一座斷頭台，底下的優勢更差。</p>"},
  verdict: {en:"Crapless is a marketing success and a math failure — unless you know the one secret: buy the 2/12 with commission-only-on-wins at ≈0.71%. Everything else about the variant charges you extra for the privilege of 'not losing' on come-out. If your cruise ship only spreads crapless, play the buy bets right or play somewhere else.",
    zh:"無敗骰是行銷的成功、數學的失敗——除非你知道那個秘密：只贏收佣的買 2/12，優勢約 0.71%。這個變體的其他一切，都是為「開骰不輸」這個特權多收錢。如果你的郵輪只開無敗骰桌，那就把買注玩對，不然就換桌玩。"}
}
);

GUIDES.push(
{
  id: "dealersecrets",
  icon: "🤫",
  title: {en:"Dealer Secrets: Rules That Change the Math", zh:"荷官不說的秘密：改變數學的規則"},
  intro: {en:"The edge isn't just in the bet — it's in the fine print. Which field paytable is on the felt, when the vig is collected, which bets can nap through a roll. Dealers know all of it; most players never ask. These are the five details worth knowing.",
    zh:"莊家優勢不只在注種裡，也在細則裡。賭桌上是哪種場注賠付表、佣金何時收、哪些注可以睡過一擲。荷官全都知道，多數玩家從沒問過。這裡是五個值得知道的細節。"},
  sections: [
    {h:{en:"Secret 1: the 0.71% bet almost nobody knows", zh:"秘密一：幾乎沒人知道的 0.71% 注"},
     body:{en:"<p>On a crapless table, <b>buy the 2 or 12 with commission charged only on wins</b>: pays 119:20 at ≈<b>0.71%</b> edge. That's better than a regular place 6/8 (1.52%) and within shouting distance of a pass line with odds. Buy the 3/11 the same way: 59:20 at ≈<b>1.25%</b>.</p><p>Almost no casual player knows this exists — it's not on any strategy card, and the table signage won't explain it. You have to ask for it: 'buy the 2, commission only on the win.' If the house charges the vig upfront instead, the edge jumps to ≈4.76% and the secret evaporates — so confirm the rule first, every time.</p>",
           zh:"<p>在無敗骰桌上，<b>買 2 或 12，且佣金只在贏時收</b>：賠 119:20，優勢約 <b>0.71%</b>。比一般置注 6/8（1.52%）還好，接近有賠率注的過關線。3/11 同樣買法：賠 59:20，優勢約 <b>1.25%</b>。</p><p>幾乎沒有散客知道這個注存在——策略卡上沒有，桌邊告示也不會解釋。你得自己開口：「buy the 2，佣金只在贏的時候收。」如果賭場是預收佣金，優勢直接跳到約 4.76%，秘密就沒了——所以每次先確認規則。</p>"}},
    {h:{en:"Secret 2: buy vs place — the vig decides", zh:"秘密二：買注 vs 置注——佣金決定一切"},
     body:{en:"<p>On a regular table, buying the 4 or 10 gets you <b>true odds (2:1)</b> instead of the place bet's short 9:5. The price is a 5% commission — and <i>when</i> it's collected changes everything:</p><ul><li><b>Vig upfront</b> (paid when you place the bet): edge <b>4.76%</b> — barely better than placing at 6.67%.</li><li><b>Vig only on wins</b>: edge ≈<b>1.7%</b> — now it's genuinely competitive with place 6/8.</li></ul><p>Some houses only offer one version; some let regulars get the good one. Ask. The difference between 4.76% and 1.7% is the difference between a sucker bet and a smart one — on the exact same number.</p>",
           zh:"<p>在一般賭桌上，買 4 或 10 拿到的是<b>真實賠率（2:1）</b>，而不是置注打折的 9:5。代價是 5% 佣金——而<i>何時收</i>決定一切：</p><ul><li><b>預收佣金</b>（下注時就付）：優勢 <b>4.76%</b>——只比置注的 6.67% 好一點。</li><li><b>只在贏時收佣</b>：優勢約 <b>1.7%</b>——這下真的能跟置注 6/8 一拚。</li></ul><p>有些賭場只提供一種，有些會給熟客好的版本。開口問。4.76% 和 1.7% 的差別，就是冤大頭注和聰明注的差別——在同一個數字上。</p>"}},
    {h:{en:"Secret 3: read the field paytable on the felt", zh:"秘密三：看賭桌上的場注賠付表"},
     body:{en:"<p>The field looks identical everywhere, but the fine print moves the edge by half:</p><ul><li><b>2:1 on both 2 AND 12:</b> edge <b>5.56%</b> — the common version.</li><li><b>3:1 on the 12</b> (or on the 2): edge <b>2.78%</b> — literally half the price.</li></ul><p>It's printed right on the layout — 'pays double on 2 and 12' vs 'pays triple on 12.' A $10 field bet on the 12 pays $20 on the first table and <b>$30</b> on the second. Check before you bet, not after. Cruise ships vary; I've seen both on the same sailing.</p>",
           zh:"<p>場注每桌看起來都一樣，但細則讓優勢差一半：</p><ul><li><b>2 和 12 都賠 2 倍：</b>優勢 <b>5.56%</b>——常見版本。</li><li><b>12 賠 3 倍</b>（或 2 賠 3 倍）：優勢 <b>2.78%</b>——直接半價。</li></ul><p>就印在賭桌版面上——「2 和 12 賠雙倍」vs「12 賠三倍」。$10 場注中 12，第一種賠 $20，第二種賠 <b>$30</b>。下注前看，不要下完才看。郵輪上兩種都見過，同一航次都可能不一樣。</p>"}},
    {h:{en:"Secret 4: working vs off — bets that can nap", zh:"秘密四：Working vs Off——可以睡覺的注"},
     body:{en:"<p>Not every bet has to sweat every roll:</p><ul><li><b>Buy bets can be turned OFF</b> (not working) during the point phase — your money naps through rolls you don't like.</li><li><b>Lay bets are ALWAYS working</b> — no naps, ever.</li><li><b>Come odds can also be turned off.</b></li><li>Place bets and odds are <b>off on the come-out</b> by default — free protection unless you ask for them working.</li></ul><p>Say 'my buy bets are off' or 'odds off, please' clearly — on a loud table the dealer won't guess. The simulator has working/off toggles for exactly these bets, because real tables do.</p>",
           zh:"<p>不是每種注都得每擲提心吊膽：</p><ul><li><b>買注可以關閉</b>（Off，不生效），在點數階段讓你的錢睡過不想玩的擲骰。</li><li><b>放注永遠生效</b>——沒得睡，永遠。</li><li><b>來注的賠率注也可以關。</b></li><li>置注和賠率注在開骰時<b>預設關閉</b>——免費保護，除非你要求開著。</li></ul><p>在吵雜的賭桌上要講清楚：「我的買注關掉」或「賠率注關一下」，荷官不會猜。模擬器給這些注做了 working/off 開關，因為真實賭桌就是這樣。</p>"}},
    {h:{en:"Secret 5: lay bets — the don't-side mirror", zh:"秘密五：放注——反向的鏡像"},
     body:{en:"<p>A <b>lay bet</b> is betting a number will <i>lose</i>: lay the 4, win if the 7 comes first, paid at true odds <b>1:2</b> (bet $40 to win $20). Edge ≈<b>2.44%</b> — the don't-side equivalent of a buy bet, minus the commission structure.</p><p>Useful if you play the don't side and want action on specific numbers. Remember secret 4: lay bets are always working, so there's no turning them off when the table gets choppy.</p>",
           zh:"<p><b>放注</b>是賭某個數字會<i>輸</i>：放注 4，7 先出現就贏，按真實賠率 <b>1:2</b> 支付（下 $40 贏 $20）。優勢約 <b>2.44%</b>——反向世界裡對應買注的存在，只是沒有佣金結構。</p><p>玩反向、想在特定號碼上加碼時好用。記住秘密四：放注永遠生效，桌況亂的時候關不掉。</p>"}}
  ],
  mathBox: {en:"<b>Dealer-secret numbers:</b><table><tr><th>Detail</th><th>Number</th></tr><tr><td>Crapless buy 2/12, vig on wins</td><td>≈0.71% edge</td></tr><tr><td>Crapless buy 3/11, vig on wins</td><td>≈1.25% edge</td></tr><tr><td>Buy 4/10, vig on wins</td><td>≈1.7% edge</td></tr><tr><td>Buy 4/10, vig upfront</td><td>4.76% edge</td></tr><tr><td>Field, 2x on 2 & 12</td><td>5.56% edge</td></tr><tr><td>Field, 3x on 12</td><td>2.78% edge</td></tr><tr><td>Lay 4/10</td><td>≈2.44% edge</td></tr></table><p>Buy bets: can be OFF · Lay bets: always working · Come odds: can be OFF.</p>",
    zh:"<b>荷官秘密數字：</b><table><tr><th>細節</th><th>數字</th></tr><tr><td>無敗骰買 2/12，只贏收佣</td><td>優勢 ≈0.71%</td></tr><tr><td>無敗骰買 3/11，只贏收佣</td><td>優勢 ≈1.25%</td></tr><tr><td>買 4/10，只贏收佣</td><td>優勢 ≈1.7%</td></tr><tr><td>買 4/10，預收佣金</td><td>優勢 4.76%</td></tr><tr><td>場注，2 和 12 賠 2 倍</td><td>優勢 5.56%</td></tr><tr><td>場注，12 賠 3 倍</td><td>優勢 2.78%</td></tr><tr><td>放注 4/10</td><td>優勢 ≈2.44%</td></tr></table><p>買注：可以關 · 放注：永遠生效 · 來注賠率：可以關。</p>"},
  verdict: {en:"The secrets aren't systems — they're reading comprehension. Same number, different vig rule, half the edge. Same field bet, different paytable, half the edge. The players who last aren't the ones with the cleverest progression; they're the ones who read the felt.",
    zh:"秘密不是系統，是閱讀理解。同一個數字，佣金規則不同，優勢差一半。同一個場注，賠付表不同，優勢差一半。玩得久的不是倍注法最聰明的人，是會看賭桌的人。"}
},
{
  id: "beginners",
  icon: "🌱",
  title: {en:"Beginner's Table Guide: What to Say & How to Last", zh:"新手上桌指南：怎麼說、怎麼玩得久"},
  intro: {en:"First time at a craps table is intimidating — the layout looks like an airplane cockpit and everyone seems to know the choreography. Here's the truth: dealers <i>want</i> you to ask. Use these scripts, follow the etiquette, and frame the night as buying entertainment by the hour, not hunting a jackpot.",
    zh:"第一次上花旗骰桌都會緊張——版面像飛機駕駛艙，每個人好像都會跳那支舞。真相是：荷官<i>希望</i>你問。用下面的話術，遵守禮儀，把這一晚定位成「按小時買娛樂」，不是「獵大獎」。"},
  sections: [
    {h:{en:"What to say to the dealer (scripts)", zh:"跟荷官怎麼說（話術腳本）"},
     body:{en:"<ul><li><b>Buying in:</b> lay cash on the table (never hand it to the dealer) — 'Change, please' / 'Chips, please.' Say your bets out loud and place chips in the come area yourself for line bets.</li><li><b>Placing a bet:</b> 'Place the 6 for $12, please.' 'Ten dollars on the come.' '$5 field.'</li><li><b>Odds:</b> 'Odds behind my pass line, please' — put the chips behind your line bet, slightly offset.</li><li><b>After a place bet hits:</b> 'Same bet.' / 'Press it up one unit.' / 'Press it up all the way.' / 'Regress to $6.'</li><li><b>Working/off:</b> 'My place bets are working.' / 'Odds off, please.' / 'Buy bets off.'</li><li><b>Tipping:</b> 'Two-way hard 8 for the boys' (a $2 hardway split dealer/player), or 'A $5 line bet for the dealers.' Tip when you're winning — dealers remember, and a tipped crew keeps your game smooth.</li></ul><p>Golden rule: <b>bets are placed with words and chips in the right area — the stickman moves them, not you.</b> Never reach into the layout mid-roll.</p>",
           zh:"<ul><li><b>換籌碼：</b>現金放桌上（不要直接遞給荷官）——「Change, please」/「換籌碼」。線注自己把籌碼放到來注區並大聲說出注碼。</li><li><b>下注：</b>「Place the 6 for $12, please.」「來注十塊。」「場注五塊。」</li><li><b>賠率注：</b>「過關線後面加賠率注」——籌碼放在線注後方，稍微偏一點。</li><li><b>置注中獎後：</b>「Same bet.」/「Press it up one unit.」/「Press it up all the way.」/「Regress to $6.」</li><li><b>開/關：</b>「我的置注要 working。」「賠率注關一下。」「買注關掉。」</li><li><b>打賞：</b>「Two-way hard 8 for the boys」（$2 硬式注荷官玩家對半），或「$5 過關線給荷官」。贏錢的時候賞——荷官記得，被賞的團隊會讓你的遊戲更順。</li></ul><p>黃金法則：<b>下注靠嘴巴說、籌碼放對區——棍棒手會去擺，你不要伸手。</b>骰子在動的時候手絕對不要伸進版面。</p>"}},
    {h:{en:"Table etiquette that keeps you welcome", zh:"讓你受歡迎的桌邊禮儀"},
     body:{en:"<ul><li><b>Hands up when the dice are out.</b> Keep hands out of the layout while the shooter rolls — the #1 beginner tell.</li><li><b>One hand on the dice.</b> When it's your roll: one hand, toss to the far wall, don't throw past the dealers.</li><li><b>Don't say 'seven'</b> at the table — superstition, but free to respect.</li><li><b>Bet on time.</b> Get bets down before the shooter has the dice; late bets get waved off.</li><li><b>Don't play the don'ts loudly</b> on a hot table — you're allowed, but read the room.</li><li><b>Tip the crew</b> when you can. On a cruise, those dealers work long contracts; a small tip goes a long way.</li></ul>",
           zh:"<ul><li><b>骰子出手時手舉高。</b>擲骰時手不要放在版面上方——新手第一大破綻。</li><li><b>拿骰子只用一隻手。</b>輪到你擲：單手，丟到對面牆，不要越過荷官丟。</li><li><b>桌上不要說「seven」</b>——迷信，但尊重不用錢。</li><li><b>準時下注。</b>擲骰者拿到骰子前把注下好；遲了會被揮掉。</li><li><b>熱桌時別大聲玩反向</b>——可以玩，但看氣氛。</li><li><b>能力所及就打賞。</b>郵輪上荷官合約長工時久，一點小費很有感。</li></ul>"}},
    {h:{en:"Beginner mistakes checklist", zh:"新手錯誤檢查表"},
     body:{en:"<p>The full 10-item checklist with explanations lives in the Practice tab — the greatest hits:</p><ul><li>Taking Big 6/8 (9.09%) instead of placing 6/8 (1.52%).</li><li>Living on any-seven / horn / hop props (12.5–16.67% edges).</li><li>Thinking numbers are 'due' — every roll is independent.</li><li>Skipping free odds — leaving 0%-edge money on the table.</li><li>Martingale with no table-max plan.</li><li>Hedging both sides to 'not lose' — paying two edges.</li><li>Playing crapless pass at 5.38% without knowing it.</li><li>Never collecting — pigs get slaughtered.</li><li>No stop-loss, no win goal.</li><li>Paying for dice-setting 'systems' — no evidence it beats the edge.</li></ul>",
           zh:"<p>完整 10 項檢查表附解說在練習分頁——精華版：</p><ul><li>下大 6/8（9.09%）而不是置注 6/8（1.52%）。</li><li>靠任意七點/號角/跳注過活（優勢 12.5–16.67%）。</li><li>覺得數字「該來了」——每次擲骰都是獨立的。</li><li>不下免費賠率注——把 0% 的錢留在桌上。</li><li>玩馬丁格爾卻沒想過桌檯上限。</li><li>兩邊對沖求「不輸」——付兩次優勢。</li><li>不知道無敗骰過關線是 5.38% 就玩。</li><li>從不收錢——豬註定被宰。</li><li>沒有停損、沒有停利。</li><li>花錢學擲骰「技術」——沒有證據能打贏莊家優勢。</li></ul>"}},
    {h:{en:"How to play all day: the honest framing", zh:"怎麼玩一整天：誠實的框架"},
     body:{en:"<p>Forget 'win big.' The achievable goal is <b>hours of entertainment at a known hourly price</b>. Rough math: ~50 rolls/hour (a realistic full-table pace) × your average total bet × the blended edge = your expected hourly cost. Example: $60 of Iron Cross action at ~3.5% ≈ <b>$2.10 per roll in expectation × 50 rolls ≈ $105/hour</b> of theoretical cost — versus $30 of 3-Point Molly action at ~0.4% ≈ <b>$6/hour</b>. Same table, same fun, 17x cheaper entertainment.</p><p>The play-all-day recipe: <b>low-edge bets</b> (pass/come + odds), <b>small units</b> relative to bankroll (50+ base units for the session), a <b>win goal</b> (leave up 30–50%) and a <b>stop-loss</b> (leave down 50%) decided <i>before</i> the first roll, and <b>collect regularly</b>. On a cruise, the casino is steps from your cabin — the easiest way to protect a winning session is to walk upstairs.</p><p>And the comps: craps earns comps slower than slots, but steady rated play still gets you the casino rate, the free drinks, the host's attention. Play for the night out; let the comps be a bonus, not the goal.</p>",
           zh:"<p>忘掉「大贏」。可實現的目標是<b>用已知的每小時價格買幾小時娛樂</b>。粗算：每小時約 50 擲（滿桌的真實節奏）× 平均總注碼 × 綜合優勢＝每小時期望成本。例子：$60 的鐵十字陣型約 3.5% ≈ 每擲期望 <b>$2.10 × 50 擲 ≈ 每小時 $105</b> 理論成本——對比 $30 的 Three Point Molly 約 0.4% ≈ <b>每小時 $6</b>。同一張桌，同樣的樂趣，17 倍便宜的娛樂。</p><p>玩一整天的配方：<b>低優勢注</b>（過關線/來注＋賠率）、<b>小單位</b>（session 賭本 50 個基本單位以上）、<b>停利目標</b>（贏 30–50% 走人）和<b>停損</b>（輸 50% 走人）——都在<i>第一擲之前</i>決定好，以及<b>定時收錢</b>。在郵輪上，賭場離房間就幾步——保護獲利 session 最簡單的方法是走上樓。</p><p>還有 comps：花旗骰攢 comps 比老虎機慢，但穩定的 rated play 照樣有賭場房價、免費飲料、host 的關照。為那一晚的娛樂而玩；讓 comps 當紅利，不要當目標。</p>"}}
  ],
  mathBox: {en:"<b>Cost of an hour (expected):</b><p>rolls/hour × avg total bet × blended edge</p><table><tr><th>Style ($60 action)</th><th>Blended edge</th><th>≈ $/hour</th></tr><tr><td>3-Point Molly + 3-4-5x</td><td>≈0.4%</td><td>≈$12</td></tr><tr><td>Place 6/8 only</td><td>1.52%</td><td>≈$46</td></tr><tr><td>Iron Cross</td><td>≈3.5%</td><td>≈$105</td></tr></table><p>Same table, same dice — the only variable is what you bet and how much. (At ~50 rolls/hour — a realistic full-table pace.)</p>",
    zh:"<b>每小時成本（期望值）：</b><p>每小時擲骰數 × 平均總注碼 × 綜合優勢</p><table><tr><th>玩法（$60 注碼）</th><th>綜合優勢</th><th>約每小時</th></tr><tr><td>Three Point Molly＋3-4-5 倍</td><td>≈0.4%</td><td>≈$12</td></tr><tr><td>只置注 6/8</td><td>1.52%</td><td>≈$46</td></tr><tr><td>鐵十字</td><td>≈3.5%</td><td>≈$105</td></tr></table><p>同一張桌，同樣的骰子——唯一的變數是你下什麼、下多少。（以每小時約 50 擲計——滿桌的真實節奏。）</p>"},
  verdict: {en:"Nobody remembers the system you played; everybody remembers whether the night was fun. Learn the scripts, respect the table, bet the cheap seats, set your walk-away numbers before the dice come out — and you'll play all day on a bankroll that used to last an hour.",
    zh:"沒人記得你玩什麼系統；人人都記得那晚好不好玩。學好話術，尊重賭桌，坐便宜的位子，骰子出手前先定好走人數字——以前一小時燒掉的賭本，現在能玩一整天。"}
}
);

GUIDES.push(
{
  id: "advantage",
  icon: "🎯",
  title: {en:"Advantage Play: The Honest Truth About Beating Craps", zh:"優勢打法：關於打敗花旗骰的誠實真相"},
  intro: {en:"Every other game on this site family has a countable angle — baccarat's Dragon 7, blackjack's Hi-Lo. Craps doesn't. This tab says that out loud, then covers what advantage-adjacent play actually exists: bonus-bet paytables, dice control claims, variance hedges, and picking the right table. The value here isn't finding an edge. It's knowing exactly how much the entertainment costs.",
    zh:"這個網站家族的其他遊戲都有可算的切入點——百家樂的龍 7、二十一點的 Hi-Lo。花旗骰沒有。這個分頁把這句話講清楚，然後談真正存在的「優勢相關」打法：紅利注賠付表、控骰說法、降波動對沖、選對賭桌。這裡的價值不是找到優勢，而是精確知道娛樂的代價。"},
  sections: [
    {h:{en:"The headline: there is no +EV bet on a craps table", zh:"開門見山：花旗骰桌上沒有正期望值注"},
     body:{en:"<p>Baccarat has Dragon 7 and Panda 8 — side bets whose edges flip positive at high counts, countable with a Hi-Lo-style system. Blackjack has card counting, full stop. <b>Craps has nothing like that.</b> Every bet on the layout has a fixed, printed edge: pass 1.41%, place 6/8 1.52%, ATS 7.76%, any seven 16.67%. No count, no trigger, no shoe composition changes any of them — the dice have no memory and every roll is 36 fresh combinations.</p><p>Anyone selling a 'craps advantage system' is selling one of three things: a progression (rearranges <i>when</i> you lose), a hedge (pays the house twice), or dice control (see below). None of them moves the edge column. Saying this plainly is the whole point of this tab — the advantage play in craps is purely <b>defensive</b>: shrink the bleed per dollar, per hour, per trip.</p>",
           zh:"<p>百家樂有龍 7 和熊貓 8——高計數時優勢翻正的邊注，可以用類 Hi-Lo 系統算。二十一點有算牌，不用多說。<b>花旗骰沒有這種東西。</b>賭桌上每個注的優勢都是固定、印好的：過關線 1.41%、置注 6/8 1.52%、ATS 7.76%、任意七點 16.67%。沒有計數、沒有觸發點、沒有牌序能改變其中任何一個——骰子沒有記憶，每擲都是全新的 36 種組合。</p><p>任何販賣「花旗骰優勢系統」的人，賣的都是三種東西之一：倍注法（重新排列你<i>何時</i>輸）、對沖（讓賭場收兩次錢）、或控骰（見下）。沒有一個能動到優勢那一欄。把這句話講白就是這個分頁的全部意義——花旗骰的優勢打法純粹是<b>防守型</b>：把每塊錢、每小時、每趟的失血壓到最小。</p>"}},
    {h:{en:"Bonus bets: could any paytable ever go +EV?", zh:"紅利注：有沒有賠付表能翻成正期望值？"},
     body:{en:"<p>This is the question advantage players actually ask about ATS, Fire, and Repeater — not 'are they fun' (they are) but 'is there a paytable anywhere that makes them +EV?' The honest answer: <b>not at any paytable I've ever seen printed.</b></p><p><b>ATS:</b> at the standard 34:1 / 174:1, edge ≈7.76%. To break even, the pays would need to be roughly <b>37:1 / 190:1</b> — and no casino prints that, because the bet exists precisely to be a lottery ticket. Some houses pay 35:1 / 175:1; the edge barely moves (≈7.4%). It's never close.</p><p><b>Fire bet:</b> at 24 / 249 / 999 for 4/5/6 points, edge ≈20%+. You'd need the top pays roughly <i>doubled</i> to sniff breakeven. Nobody offers that.</p><p><b>Repeater:</b> paytables vary by table, which is exactly why you check — but the family resemblance (ATS, Fire) tells you the pricing philosophy. If the paytable isn't printed on the felt, that's your answer.</p><p>The takeaway isn't 'never play them.' A $1 ATS is a fine dollar of entertainment. The takeaway is: <b>no paytable turns them into an investment</b>, so size them like lottery tickets — tiny, for fun, zero expectation.</p>",
           zh:"<p>這是優勢玩家真正會問 ATS、Fire、Repeater 的問題——不是「好不好玩」（好玩），而是「有沒有哪個賠付表能讓它們變正期望值？」誠實的答案：<b>我見過的印製品裡沒有。</b></p><p><b>ATS：</b>標準 34:1 / 174:1，優勢約 7.76%。要打平，賠付大概要 <b>37:1 / 190:1</b>——沒有賭場會印這個，因為這個注的存在目的就是當樂透。有些賭場賠 35:1 / 175:1，優勢幾乎不動（約 7.4%）。永遠差得遠。</p><p><b>Fire 注：</b>4/5/6 個點數賠 24 / 249 / 999，優勢約 20%+。最高賠付大概要<i>翻倍</i>才摸得到打平邊。沒人這樣開。</p><p><b>Repeater：</b>賠付表每桌不同，這正是要你先看的原因——但它跟 ATS、Fire 是同一家族，定價哲學都一樣。賠付表沒印在賭桌上，那就是答案。</p><p>結論不是「永遠別玩」。$1 的 ATS 是花得起的一塊錢娛樂。結論是：<b>沒有賠付表能把它們變成投資</b>，所以下注規模就按樂透處理——小注、好玩、零期待。</p>"}},
    {h:{en:"Dice control: the fair, skeptical take", zh:"控骰：公平但懷疑的看法"},
     body:{en:"<p><b>What shooters claim:</b> with a consistent grip, toss arc, and landing zone — dice landing softly, hitting the back wall but not tumbling randomly — a practiced shooter can influence the outcome: fewer sevens, more on-axis numbers. The controlled-throw community has books, seminars, and true believers.</p><p><b>What the math says:</b> no controlled study has ever demonstrated a <i>beatable, repeatable</i> player edge from dice setting. The back-wall requirement exists precisely to randomize; even a small genuine influence would need thousands of documented throws to separate from luck, and that dataset doesn't exist in public. Casinos <i>allow</i> dice setting — which tells you what they think of it. If it threatened them, the dice would have to tumble like popcorn.</p><p><b>The fair middle:</b> a smooth, consistent throw probably doesn't hurt, and the discipline of a pre-shot routine keeps <i>you</i> calmer — which is worth something at a table designed to excite you. But betting money on the belief that you're beating 1.41% with your wrist is the most expensive grip in the casino. Treat it as craft, not edge.</p>",
           zh:"<p><b>控骰者說什麼：</b>用固定的握法、拋物線、落點——骰子輕輕落地，碰到後牆但不亂滾——練過的擲骰者能影響結果：少一點 7，多一點軸線數字。控骰圈有書、有研討會、有真信徒。</p><p><b>數學說什麼：</b>從來沒有受控研究證明過控骰能產生<i>可打敗、可重複</i>的玩家優勢。後牆規則的存在就是為了隨機化；即使真有微小影響，也需要幾千次有記錄的投擲才能跟運氣區分開，而這個數據集公開不存在。賭場<i>允許</i>擺骰——這就說明了他們的看法。真有威脅的話，骰子早被要求像爆米花一樣亂彈了。</p><p><b>公平的中間立場：</b>平穩一致的投擲大概無害，投擲前的固定儀式也能讓<i>你</i>更冷靜——在專門設計來讓你興奮的賭桌上，這有它的價值。但拿錢去賭「我的手腕能打敗 1.41%」，是賭場裡最貴的握法。把它當工藝，不要當優勢。</p>"}},
    {h:{en:"Hedges that calm the ride (not the edge)", zh:"讓過程平穩的對沖（不是降低優勢）"},
     body:{en:"<p>The hedge tab on this site proves the math: every hedge is two bets, and the house collects on both. But there's an honest, smaller claim some hedges can make — <b>variance reduction</b>. A Don't Pass bet with full odds, for example, wins small often and loses big rarely; pairing a small lay hedge against a place-bet-heavy layout smooths the cliffs without pretending to beat anything.</p><p>The rule stays iron: <b>lower variance ≠ lower edge.</b> A 'Don't Pass + lay the 4 and 10' position feels serene because the 7 — the most common roll — is suddenly your friend. You're still paying 1.36% on the flat and ~2.44% on the lays for that serenity. That's a fair trade <i>if you know the price</i> — it's buying a calmer session, not a winning one.</p><p>If calm is what you want, the cheapest version is simply smaller bets on one side. Every hedge dollar is a dollar paying full edge for psychological comfort. Sometimes that's worth it. Just label it correctly in your head.</p>",
           zh:"<p>本站的對沖分頁已經證明了數學：每個對沖都是兩筆注，賭場兩筆都收錢。但有些對沖能提出一個更小、更誠實的主張——<b>降低波動</b>。例如不過關加滿賠率注：小贏頻繁、大輸罕見；用小額放注去對沖重置注的版面，能把斷崖磨平，但不假裝能打敗什麼。</p><p>鐵律不變：<b>低波動 ≠ 低優勢。</b>「不過關＋放注 4 和 10」的部位感覺很平靜，因為最常見的 7 突然變成你的朋友。但這份平靜的代價是本注 1.36%、放注約 2.44% 照付。<i>知道價格的話</i>這是公平交易——你買的是更平穩的 session，不是會贏的 session。</p><p>如果要的就是平靜，最便宜的版本是單邊下小注。每一塊對沖的錢，都是用全額優勢買心理舒適。有時值得。但在心裡要標對價籤。</p>"}},
    {h:{en:"Table selection: pick your battlefield", zh:"選桌：選你的戰場"},
     body:{en:"<p>Since you can't change the edges, change the <i>table</i>. Five things to check before you buy in — the dealer's-secrets tab has the full numbers, this is the checklist:</p><ul><li><b>Odds multiple:</b> 10x beats 3-4-5x beats 2x. Blended edge on a 3-Point Molly: ≈0.4% → ≈0.18% → ≈0.02% at 100x. More odds = cheaper entertainment.</li><li><b>Field paytable:</b> 12 pays triple (2.78%) vs double on 2 and 12 (5.56%). Read the felt before you bet.</li><li><b>Crapless vs regular:</b> regular, always — unless you know the crapless buy-2/12 secret (0.71%, vig-on-wins only) and the table actually offers it.</li><li><b>Buy vig rule:</b> 'commission only on wins' (≈1.7% on the 4/10) vs upfront (4.76%). Ask the dealer; the answer is worth 3%.</li><li><b>ATS/Fire availability:</b> if you play them for fun, confirm the paytable is printed. No printed paytable = no bet.</li></ul><p>On a cruise ship you often get one table and no choice — then the checklist becomes a bet-selection guide instead. The table you can't change still tells you which bets to avoid.</p>",
           zh:"<p>既然改變不了優勢，那就改變<i>賭桌</i>。買籌碼前先檢查五件事——荷官秘密分頁有完整數字，這裡是檢查清單：</p><ul><li><b>賠率注倍數：</b>10 倍勝過 3-4-5 倍勝過 2 倍。Three Point Molly 綜合優勢：約 0.4% → 約 0.18% → 100 倍約 0.02%。賠率注越多，娛樂越便宜。</li><li><b>場注賠付表：</b>12 賠三倍（2.78%）vs 2 和 12 賠雙倍（5.56%）。下注前先看賭桌版面。</li><li><b>無敗骰 vs 一般桌：</b>永遠選一般桌——除非你知道無敗骰買 2/12 的秘密（0.71%，只贏收佣）而且該桌真的這樣開。</li><li><b>買注佣金規則：</b>「只在贏時收」（4/10 約 1.7%）vs 預收（4.76%）。問荷官；答案值 3%。</li><li><b>ATS/Fire 有沒有開：</b>如果純好玩想下，先確認賠付表有印出來。沒印＝不下。</li></ul><p>郵輪上常常只有一桌沒得選——那這份清單就變成選注指南。不能換的桌，至少告訴你哪些注要避開。</p>"}}
  ],
  mathBox: {en:"<b>The defensive player's price list:</b><table><tr><th>Choice</th><th>Edge</th></tr><tr><td>Pass + 3-4-5x odds (blended)</td><td>≈0.3–0.5%</td></tr><tr><td>Pass + 10x odds (blended)</td><td>≈0.18%</td></tr><tr><td>Crapless buy 2/12, vig on wins</td><td>≈0.71%</td></tr><tr><td>Place 6/8</td><td>1.52%</td></tr><tr><td>Field (12 pays 3x)</td><td>2.78%</td></tr><tr><td>Field (2x on 2 & 12)</td><td>5.56%</td></tr><tr><td>ATS (any paytable seen)</td><td>≈7.4–7.76%</td></tr><tr><td>Fire bet</td><td>≈20%+</td></tr><tr><td>Any seven</td><td>16.67%</td></tr></table><p>No count, no trigger, no shoe: every number above is fixed. The only 'advantage' in craps is choosing the smallest number on this list.</p>",
    zh:"<b>防守型玩家的價目表：</b><table><tr><th>選擇</th><th>優勢</th></tr><tr><td>過關線＋3-4-5 倍賠率（綜合）</td><td>≈0.3–0.5%</td></tr><tr><td>過關線＋10 倍賠率（綜合）</td><td>≈0.18%</td></tr><tr><td>無敗骰買 2/12，只贏收佣</td><td>≈0.71%</td></tr><tr><td>置注 6/8</td><td>1.52%</td></tr><tr><td>場注（12 賠三倍）</td><td>2.78%</td></tr><tr><td>場注（2 和 12 賠雙倍）</td><td>5.56%</td></tr><tr><td>ATS（見過的任何賠付表）</td><td>≈7.4–7.76%</td></tr><tr><td>Fire 注</td><td>≈20%+</td></tr><tr><td>任意七點</td><td>16.67%</td></tr></table><p>沒有計數、沒有觸發點、沒有牌序：上面的每個數字都是固定的。花旗骰唯一的「優勢」，就是選這張表上最小的數字。</p>"},
  verdict: {en:"Craps will never give you a Dragon 7 — no bet on the felt flips positive, no matter how you count, because there's nothing to count. What it gives you instead is a menu with the prices printed on it. The players who last decades aren't the ones with a secret throw; they're the ones who read the menu, pick the cheapest items, and enjoy the meal. That's the whole advantage play. It's enough.",
    zh:"花旗骰永遠不會給你龍 7——賭桌上沒有任何注會翻成正期望值，怎麼算都一樣，因為根本沒東西可算。它給你的是一份印好價格的菜單。玩幾十年的人不是有秘密投擲法的人，是會看菜單、點最便宜的菜、好好享受這餐的人。這就是全部的優勢打法。這樣就夠了。"}
}
);

